  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are constrained by a very small volume of academic literature meeting the inclusion criteria, limiting the depth of the peer-reviewed evidence base.",
      "what": "This scoping review analyzed 7 peer-reviewed papers and 38 grey literature resources, selected from an initial pool of 170 documents, to examine how safety culture and safety climate affect work-related driving.",
      "why": "The review reveals a disconnect in workplace road safety responsibility: while grey literature emphasizes that managers and leaders hold legislative duties, peer-reviewed academic studies tend to focus disproportionately on individual driver behavior rather than leadership's role in fostering a safe culture."
